0
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
BLACK SCREEN

1
00:02:33,790 --> 00:02:35,000
It's beautiful here.

2
00:02:36,560 --> 00:02:39,800
It was our aunt's. We used to come here as kids.

3
00:02:40,840 --> 00:02:43,580
The Order uses it now as a safe house.

4
00:02:45,180 --> 00:02:47,130
What's left of us at least.

5
00:02:49,340 --> 00:02:51,810
Muggles think these things keep evil away.

6
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:53,390
But they're wrong.

7
00:02:56,130 --> 00:02:58,250
I need to talk to the Goblin.

8
00:03:09,740 --> 00:03:11,400
How are you?

9
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:14,830
Alive.

10
00:03:20,070 --> 00:03:21,110
You probably don't remember that you...

11
00:03:21,110 --> 00:03:22,350
That I showed you to your vault,

12
00:03:22,350 --> 00:03:23,700
the first time you came to Gringotts.

13
00:03:25,040 --> 00:03:27,420
Even amongst Goblins, you are famous Harry Potter.

14
00:03:31,910 --> 00:03:33,690
You buried the elf?

15
00:03:33,690 --> 00:03:34,450
Yes.

16
00:03:35,470 --> 00:03:36,740
And brought me here.

17
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:40,400
You are...

18
00:03:42,700 --> 00:03:44,660
...pretty unusual wizard.

19
00:03:52,550 --> 00:03:54,400
How did you come by the sword?

20
00:03:59,110 --> 00:04:00,360
It's complicated.

21
00:04:02,690 --> 00:04:04,180
Why did Bellatrix Lestrange

22
00:04:04,180 --> 00:04:05,890
think it should be in her vault at Gringotts?

23
00:04:07,580 --> 00:04:10,100
It's complicated.

24
00:04:13,020 --> 00:04:16,320
The sword presented itself to us, in moment of need.

25
00:04:16,790 --> 00:04:18,190
We didn't steal it.

26
00:04:20,440 --> 00:04:23,650
There is a sword in Madam lestrange's vault

27
00:04:23,650 --> 00:04:24,770
identical to this one.

28
00:04:24,770 --> 00:04:26,110
But it is a fake.

29
00:04:27,140 --> 00:04:29,040
It was placed there this past summer.

30
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:30,740
And she never suspected it was a fake.

31
00:04:30,740 --> 00:04:32,030
The replica is very convincing.

32
00:04:32,030 --> 00:04:33,710
Only a goblin would recognize

33
00:04:33,710 --> 00:04:35,790
that this is the true Sword of Gryffindor.

34
00:04:36,330 --> 00:04:37,530
Who is the acquaintance?

35
00:04:38,370 --> 00:04:39,530
A Hogwarts Professor.

36
00:04:40,540 --> 00:04:42,570
As I understand that he's now Headmaster.

37
00:04:43,500 --> 00:04:44,390
Snape.

38
00:04:45,650 --> 00:04:47,900
He put a fake sword in Bellatrix's vault.

39
00:04:48,930 --> 00:04:49,910
Why?

40
00:04:50,190 --> 00:04:51,530
There are more than a few

41
00:04:51,530 --> 00:04:54,060
curious things in the vaults at Gringotts.

42
00:04:55,430 --> 00:04:58,120
And in Madam Lestrange's vault as well?

43
00:05:01,120 --> 00:05:02,450
Perhaps.

44
00:05:04,820 --> 00:05:06,470
I need to get into Gringotts.

45
00:05:06,470 --> 00:05:08,260
Into one of the vaults.

46
00:05:08,950 --> 00:05:10,270
It is impossible.

47
00:05:10,270 --> 00:05:11,560
Alone, yes.

48
00:05:11,930 --> 00:05:13,800
But with you, no.

49
00:05:19,380 --> 00:05:21,990
- Why should I help you? - I have gold.

50
00:05:22,640 --> 00:05:23,760
Lots of it.

51
00:05:23,910 --> 00:05:25,390
I've no interest in gold.

52
00:05:25,770 --> 00:05:26,610
Then what?

53
00:05:32,140 --> 00:05:32,970
That.

54
00:05:34,350 --> 00:05:35,790
That is my price.

55
00:05:49,230 --> 00:05:51,760
Are you thinking there's a Horcrux in Bellatrix's vault?

56
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:54,400
Well, she was terrified when she thought we had been in there.

57
00:05:54,670 --> 00:05:56,450
She kept asking you, what else was taken?

58
00:05:56,940 --> 00:05:58,920
I bet you anything, there's Horcrux in there.

59
00:05:58,920 --> 00:06:00,190
Another piece of his soul.

60
00:06:00,190 --> 00:06:01,430
Let's find it, kill it,

61
00:06:01,430 --> 00:06:03,220
and we are one step closer to killing him.

62
00:06:03,220 --> 00:06:04,450
And what happens when we find it?

63
00:06:04,450 --> 00:06:06,370
How're we supposed to destroy it,

64
00:06:06,370 --> 00:06:07,600
now you're giving the sword to Griphook?

65
00:06:08,810 --> 00:06:10,370
I'm still working on that part.

66
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:13,950
He's weak.

67
00:06:24,050 --> 00:06:24,940
Who?

68
00:06:27,030 --> 00:06:28,050
Mr. Ollivander.

69
00:06:29,170 --> 00:06:31,020
I need to ask you a few questions.

70
00:06:31,350 --> 00:06:33,310
Anything, m'boy. Anything!

71
00:06:35,340 --> 00:06:37,330
Would you mind identifying this wand?

72
00:06:37,370 --> 00:06:39,790
We need to know if it's safe to use.

73
00:06:43,430 --> 00:06:47,700
Uhh... Walnut.

74
00:06:49,110 --> 00:06:51,060
Dragon Heartstring.

75
00:06:52,410 --> 00:06:54,330
12 and three quarter inches.

76
00:06:56,020 --> 00:06:56,750
Unyie...

77
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:01,270
Unyielding.

78
00:07:02,720 --> 00:07:06,700
This belonged to Bellatrix Lestrange.

79
00:07:06,700 --> 00:07:09,140
Treat it carefully.

80
00:07:10,660 --> 00:07:11,910
And this?

81
00:07:15,520 --> 00:07:16,410
Hawthorn.

82
00:07:18,640 --> 00:07:20,280
An unicorn hair.

83
00:07:21,390 --> 00:07:22,490
10 inches.

84
00:07:23,360 --> 00:07:25,140
Reasonably pliant.

85
00:07:29,650 --> 00:07:33,280
This was the wand of Draco Malfoy.

86
00:07:34,870 --> 00:07:35,740
Was?

87
00:07:36,270 --> 00:07:37,310
Is it not still?

88
00:07:37,590 --> 00:07:40,620
Well, perhaps not. If you won it from him.

89
00:07:44,010 --> 00:07:46,770
I sense its allegiance has changed.

90
00:07:52,350 --> 00:07:56,380
You talk about wands, as if they have feelings...

91
00:07:59,160 --> 00:08:00,240
...can think!

92
00:08:03,830 --> 00:08:07,470
The wand chooses the wizard, Mr. Potter.

93
00:08:08,780 --> 00:08:10,890
That much has always been clear

94
00:08:10,890 --> 00:08:13,700
to those of us who've studied wandlore.

95
00:08:15,410 --> 00:08:18,400
And, what do you know about the Deathly Hallows?

96
00:08:23,360 --> 00:08:25,640
It is rumored there are three.

97
00:08:28,370 --> 00:08:30,640
The Elder Wand,

98
00:08:30,640 --> 00:08:33,260
the Cloak of Invisibility,

99
00:08:33,260 --> 00:08:35,810
to hide you from your enemies,

100
00:08:35,810 --> 00:08:38,430
and the Resurrection Stone,

101
00:08:38,430 --> 00:08:41,580
to bring back loved ones from the dead.

102
00:08:41,580 --> 00:08:46,910
Together, they make one the Master of Death.

103
00:08:48,010 --> 00:08:53,900
But few, truly believe that such objects exist.

104
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:54,680
Do you?

105
00:08:56,280 --> 00:08:57,660
Do you believe they exist, sir?

106
00:09:01,790 --> 00:09:07,330
I see no reason to put stock into an old wives' tale.

107
00:09:08,950 --> 00:09:09,610
You're lying!

108
00:09:11,420 --> 00:09:12,780
You know one exists.

109
00:09:13,830 --> 00:09:15,430
You told him about it.

110
00:09:15,430 --> 00:09:18,170
You told him about the Elder Wand...

111
00:09:18,640 --> 00:09:20,840
and where he could go looking for it.

112
00:09:24,680 --> 00:09:26,080
He tortured me.

113
00:09:29,610 --> 00:09:30,590
Besides...

114
00:09:32,450 --> 00:09:34,120
...I only conveyed rumors.

115
00:09:36,960 --> 00:09:37,510
There's...

116
00:09:39,860 --> 00:09:42,260
There's no telling whether he will find it.

117
00:09:45,840 --> 00:09:47,260
He has found it, sir.

118
00:09:53,650 --> 00:09:54,710
We'll let you rest.

119
00:09:57,910 --> 00:09:59,970
He's after you, Mr. Potter.

120
00:10:00,940 --> 00:10:03,350
If it's true what you say,

121
00:10:04,100 --> 00:10:06,050
that he has the Elder Wand.

122
00:10:08,450 --> 00:10:13,000
I'm afraid, you really don't stand a chance.

123
00:10:15,210 --> 00:10:17,230
Well, I suppose I'll have to kill him before he finds me, then.

124
00:10:23,800 --> 00:10:24,960
You're sure that's hers?

125
00:10:27,570 --> 00:10:28,640
Positive.

126
00:10:38,020 --> 00:10:39,110
How do I look?

127
00:10:40,270 --> 00:10:41,160
Hideous.

128
00:10:42,740 --> 00:10:45,660
You can give that to Hermione to hold. Alright, Griphook?

129
00:11:05,820 --> 00:11:07,190
We're relying on you, Griphook.

130
00:11:07,190 --> 00:11:09,100
If you get us past the guards into the vault...

131
00:11:09,100 --> 00:11:10,260
The sword's yours.

132
00:11:23,690 --> 00:11:24,880
Madam Lestrange.

133
00:11:25,080 --> 00:11:26,040
Good morning.

134
00:11:28,160 --> 00:11:31,210
Good morning? Good morning?

135
00:11:31,690 --> 00:11:34,610
You're Bellatrix Lestrange, not some juvenile school girl!

136
00:11:34,610 --> 00:11:35,790
Hey! Easy!

137
00:11:36,920 --> 00:11:38,100
If she gives us away,

138
00:11:38,100 --> 00:11:41,480
we must swear to use that sword to slit our own throats.

139
00:11:41,970 --> 00:11:43,090
Understand?

140
00:11:43,770 --> 00:11:44,860
No, he's right.

141
00:11:45,230 --> 00:11:46,520
I speak stupid.

142
00:11:47,590 --> 00:11:50,210
Okay. Let's do it.

143
00:12:55,580 --> 00:12:58,030
I wish to enter my vault.

144
00:13:01,760 --> 00:13:03,620
Identification?

145
00:13:07,090 --> 00:13:09,040
I hardly think that would be necessary.

146
00:13:12,240 --> 00:13:13,440
Madam Lestrange.

147
00:13:19,380 --> 00:13:21,110
I don't like to be kept waiting.

148
00:13:22,070 --> 00:13:23,170
I know.

149
00:13:23,940 --> 00:13:25,330
They know she's an impostor.

150
00:13:28,940 --> 00:13:30,040
They'd be warned.

151
00:13:38,620 --> 00:13:39,200
Harry.

152
00:13:40,850 --> 00:13:41,900
What do we do, Harry?

153
00:13:48,520 --> 00:13:52,060
Madam Lestrange, would you mind presenting your wand?

154
00:13:53,120 --> 00:13:54,620
And why should I do that?

155
00:13:54,620 --> 00:13:56,200
It's the bank's policy!

156
00:13:56,200 --> 00:13:59,430
I'm sure you understand, given current climate.

157
00:14:00,800 --> 00:14:03,480
No! I most certainly do not understand!

158
00:14:03,910 --> 00:14:06,920
I'm afraid, I must insist.

159
00:14:12,980 --> 00:14:13,810
Imperio!

160
00:14:20,460 --> 00:14:22,280
Very well, Madam Lestrange.

161
00:14:22,860 --> 00:14:24,000
If you will follow me?

162
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:01,700
What is that, Griphook?

163
00:15:07,340 --> 00:15:08,140
Griphook!

164
00:15:27,140 --> 00:15:28,950
Aresto Momentum.

165
00:15:33,790 --> 00:15:34,690
Well done, Hermione.

166
00:15:43,430 --> 00:15:44,880
Oh no, you two're like you again.

167
00:15:45,880 --> 00:15:49,270
The Thief's Downfall, washes away all enchantments.

168
00:15:50,040 --> 00:15:50,890
Can be deadly.

169
00:15:51,300 --> 00:15:52,010
You don't say.

170
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:55,160
Just out of interest, is there any other way out of here?

171
00:15:56,190 --> 00:15:56,940
No.

172
00:15:58,830 --> 00:16:01,980
What the devil are all you doing down here?

173
00:16:02,850 --> 00:16:03,510
Thieves!

174
00:16:04,160 --> 00:16:04,940
You gave up the...

175
00:16:04,940 --> 00:16:05,870
- Imperio. - You!

176
00:16:17,730 --> 00:16:18,670
That doesn't sound good.

177
00:16:30,390 --> 00:16:30,990
Bloody hell!

178
00:16:31,640 --> 00:16:32,810
That's an Ukrainian Ironbelly.

179
00:16:33,190 --> 00:16:33,890
Here.

180
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:47,960
It's been trained to expect pain when it hears the noise.

181
00:16:48,920 --> 00:16:50,000
That's barbaric!

182
00:17:20,180 --> 00:17:20,830
Lumos.

183
00:17:26,030 --> 00:17:27,180
Blimey!

184
00:17:34,660 --> 00:17:35,830
Accio Horcrux.

185
00:17:38,410 --> 00:17:40,090
It seems you're gonna try that one again, aren't you?

186
00:17:40,410 --> 00:17:42,120
No kind of magic would work in here.

187
00:17:47,420 --> 00:17:49,070
It's in here, Harry?

188
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:51,600
Can you feel anything?

189
00:18:13,490 --> 00:18:15,640
That's it! Up there!

190
00:18:19,610 --> 00:18:21,080
They have added the Gemino curse.

191
00:18:21,080 --> 00:18:22,640
Everything you touch will multiply.

192
00:18:23,180 --> 00:18:24,200
Give me the sword.

193
00:18:42,410 --> 00:18:43,760
Stop moving!

194
00:19:06,730 --> 00:19:07,420
Got it!

195
00:19:11,030 --> 00:19:12,580
We had a deal, Griphook!

196
00:19:12,580 --> 00:19:13,860
The cup for the sword!

197
00:19:19,780 --> 00:19:21,080
I said I'll get you in,

198
00:19:21,080 --> 00:19:23,720
I didn't say anything about getting you out.

199
00:19:45,980 --> 00:19:47,170
Griphook!

200
00:19:47,170 --> 00:19:48,000
Thieves!

201
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:48,890
Griphook!

202
00:19:49,100 --> 00:19:50,340
Thieves!

203
00:19:53,710 --> 00:19:54,700
Is that okay?

204
00:19:55,560 --> 00:19:56,570
We've still got Bogrod.

205
00:20:04,250 --> 00:20:05,250
That's unfortunate.

206
00:20:09,840 --> 00:20:11,850
We can't just stand here, you got any idea?

207
00:20:12,330 --> 00:20:13,210
You are the brilliant one.

208
00:20:13,760 --> 00:20:15,750
I've got something, but it's mad!

209
00:20:16,590 --> 00:20:17,340
Reducto.

210
00:20:30,260 --> 00:20:31,340
Well, come on, then!

211
00:20:33,950 --> 00:20:35,180
Relashio.

212
00:21:23,130 --> 00:21:23,980
Keep moving!

213
00:21:51,160 --> 00:21:52,370
Now what?

214
00:21:52,900 --> 00:21:53,900
Reducto.

215
00:21:55,670 --> 00:21:56,300
Hold on.

216
00:22:06,410 --> 00:22:09,190
That was brilliant! Absolutely brilliant!

217
00:22:37,780 --> 00:22:38,640
We're dropping!

218
00:22:42,480 --> 00:22:44,220
- I say we jump! - When?

219
00:22:44,810 --> 00:22:45,430
Now!

220
00:23:40,680 --> 00:23:41,380
He knows.

221
00:23:42,100 --> 00:23:42,840
You-Know-Who.

222
00:23:43,790 --> 00:23:45,050
He knows we broke into Gringotts.

223
00:23:45,540 --> 00:23:48,220
He knows what we took, and he knows we're hunting Horcruxes.

224
00:23:48,900 --> 00:23:50,250
- How is it you know? - I saw him.

225
00:23:50,900 --> 00:23:51,910
You let him in?

226
00:23:51,910 --> 00:23:53,470
Harry, you can't do that!

227
00:23:53,490 --> 00:23:55,060
Hermione, I can't always help it!

228
00:23:55,560 --> 00:23:57,030
Well, maybe I can. I don't know!

229
00:23:57,360 --> 00:23:58,650
Never mind! What happened?

230
00:23:58,940 --> 00:24:00,580
Well, he's angry,

231
00:24:01,170 --> 00:24:02,420
and scared too.

232
00:24:02,420 --> 00:24:03,850
He knows, if we find and destroy

233
00:24:03,850 --> 00:24:05,570
all the Horcruxes, we'll be able to kill him.

234
00:24:06,350 --> 00:24:07,500
I reckon he'll stop at nothing

235
00:24:07,500 --> 00:24:08,840
to make sure we don't find the rest.

236
00:24:11,190 --> 00:24:12,200
And there's more.

237
00:24:12,200 --> 00:24:13,380
One of them is at Hogwarts.

238
00:24:13,670 --> 00:24:14,570
What?

239
00:24:15,370 --> 00:24:16,260
You saw it?

240
00:24:16,260 --> 00:24:17,160
I saw the castle,

241
00:24:17,160 --> 00:24:18,190
and Rowena Ravenclaw.

242
00:24:18,370 --> 00:24:19,690
It must have something to do with her.

243
00:24:19,690 --> 00:24:20,800
We have to go there, now!

244
00:24:21,150 --> 00:24:22,230
Well, we can't do that!

245
00:24:22,880 --> 00:24:24,690
We've got to plan, we've got to figure it out!

246
00:24:24,690 --> 00:24:27,620
Hermione, when have any of our plans ever actually worked?

247
00:24:27,880 --> 00:24:29,830
We plan, we get there, all hell breaks loose.

248
00:24:31,400 --> 00:24:33,490
He's right! One problem.

249
00:24:34,310 --> 00:24:35,180
Snape's Headmaster now,

250
00:24:35,180 --> 00:24:37,030
we can't just move from the front door!

251
00:24:38,450 --> 00:24:41,960
Well, we'll go to Hogsmeade, to Honeydukes.

252
00:24:42,220 --> 00:24:43,570
Take the secret passage in the cellar.

253
00:24:44,710 --> 00:24:45,490
It's...

254
00:24:45,910 --> 00:24:47,230
There's something wrong with him.

255
00:24:48,200 --> 00:24:49,450
It's like, you know, in the past,

256
00:24:50,500 --> 00:24:52,190
I've always been able to follow his thoughts.

257
00:24:52,810 --> 00:24:54,570
And now everything just feels disconnected.

258
00:24:55,780 --> 00:24:56,640
Maybe it's the Horcruxes.

259
00:24:56,640 --> 00:24:57,990
Maybe he's growing weaker.

260
00:24:58,000 --> 00:24:58,850
Maybe he's dying!

261
00:24:59,190 --> 00:25:00,120
No!

262
00:25:00,230 --> 00:25:01,760
No, it's...it's more like he's wounded.

263
00:25:02,670 --> 00:25:04,310
If anything, he feels more dangerous.

264
00:25:55,160 --> 00:25:56,720
- Right here. Come on! - Search everywhere.

265
00:26:17,050 --> 00:26:18,730
Faster!

266
00:26:31,810 --> 00:26:32,730
In here, Potter.

267
00:26:46,820 --> 00:26:47,710
Did you look at him?

268
00:26:48,860 --> 00:26:50,180
For a second I thought that was...

269
00:26:50,180 --> 00:26:51,510
I know. Dumbledore!

270
00:27:08,240 --> 00:27:08,830
Harry?

271
00:27:11,480 --> 00:27:12,790
I can see you in this.

272
00:27:26,740 --> 00:27:29,310
Bloody fools, what were you thinking, coming here?

273
00:27:29,740 --> 00:27:31,980
Have you any idea how dangerous it is?

274
00:27:32,120 --> 00:27:34,810
You're Aberforth, Dumbledore's brother.

275
00:27:36,450 --> 00:27:37,910
It's you who I've been seeing in here.

276
00:27:39,110 --> 00:27:40,180
You're the one who sent Dobby.

277
00:27:40,800 --> 00:27:43,110
- Why've you left him? - He's dead.

278
00:27:44,430 --> 00:27:46,220
Sorry to hear it. I liked that elf.

279
00:27:46,500 --> 00:27:47,410
Who gave that to you?

280
00:27:47,740 --> 00:27:48,370
The mirror?

281
00:27:50,040 --> 00:27:52,430
Mundungus Fletcher, 'bout a year ago.

282
00:27:52,440 --> 00:27:54,010
Dung had no right selling that to you.

283
00:27:54,010 --> 00:27:54,910
- It belongs to... - Sirius...

284
00:27:56,340 --> 00:27:57,560
Albus told me.

285
00:27:58,620 --> 00:28:01,290
He also told me you'd likely be hacked off,

286
00:28:01,550 --> 00:28:03,090
if you ever found that I had it.

287
00:28:03,090 --> 00:28:04,240
But, ask yourself:

288
00:28:04,990 --> 00:28:07,010
Where would you be if I didn't?

289
00:28:11,200 --> 00:28:12,170
Do you have any others much?

290
00:28:12,520 --> 00:28:13,170
From the Order?

291
00:28:13,920 --> 00:28:15,020
The Order's finished.

292
00:28:16,010 --> 00:28:17,050
You-Know-Who's won,

293
00:28:17,660 --> 00:28:20,580
anyone who says otherwise is killing themselves.

294
00:28:21,120 --> 00:28:23,350
We need to get into Hogwarts, tonight.

295
00:28:24,190 --> 00:28:25,530
Dumbledore gave us a job to do.

296
00:28:25,970 --> 00:28:26,880
Did he now...

297
00:28:27,830 --> 00:28:30,060
Nice job? Easy?

298
00:28:30,890 --> 00:28:32,240
We've been hunting Horcruxes.

299
00:28:33,620 --> 00:28:35,480
And we think the last one's inside the castle.

300
00:28:35,590 --> 00:28:37,080
But we'll need your help getting in.

301
00:28:37,090 --> 00:28:40,640
Which job my brother has given you now, it's a suicide mission.

302
00:28:40,960 --> 00:28:42,880
Do yourself a favor, boy. Go home!

303
00:28:43,430 --> 00:28:44,310
Live a little longer.

304
00:28:44,510 --> 00:28:46,160
Dumbledore trusted me to see this through.

305
00:28:46,310 --> 00:28:48,180
What makes you think you can trust him?

306
00:28:49,570 --> 00:28:50,500
What makes you think you

307
00:28:50,500 --> 00:28:52,080
can believe anything my brother told you?

308
00:28:52,340 --> 00:28:53,350
And in all the time you knew him...

309
00:28:54,040 --> 00:28:55,490
did he ever mention my name?

310
00:28:57,020 --> 00:28:58,450
Did he ever mentioned hers?

311
00:28:59,290 --> 00:29:00,990
- Why should he... - Keep secrets.

312
00:29:00,990 --> 00:29:02,430
You tell me?

313
00:29:04,010 --> 00:29:06,460
- I trusted him. - That's a boy's answer.

314
00:29:07,820 --> 00:29:09,560
A boy goes chasing Horcruxes on the

315
00:29:09,560 --> 00:29:12,340
word of a man who wouldn't even tell him where to start.

316
00:29:12,600 --> 00:29:13,400
You're lying!

317
00:29:14,470 --> 00:29:16,830
Not just on me, that doesn't matter.

318
00:29:16,830 --> 00:29:18,010
To yourself as well.

319
00:29:18,440 --> 00:29:19,680
That's what a fool does.

320
00:29:20,590 --> 00:29:24,130
You don't strike me as a fool, Harry Potter!

321
00:29:24,690 --> 00:29:28,180
So, I'll ask you again, there must be a reason.

322
00:29:31,220 --> 00:29:33,420
I'm not interested in what happened between you and your brother.

323
00:29:35,250 --> 00:29:36,680
I don't care that you've given up.

324
00:29:39,920 --> 00:29:41,490
I trusted the man I knew.

325
00:29:45,670 --> 00:29:47,300
We need to get into the castle tonight.

326
00:29:54,080 --> 00:29:55,430
You know what to do.

327
00:30:03,070 --> 00:30:04,010
Where've you sent her?

328
00:30:05,460 --> 00:30:06,180
You'll see.

329
00:30:07,230 --> 00:30:08,170
Soon enough.

330
00:30:15,380 --> 00:30:17,050
That's your sister, Ariana. Isn't it?

331
00:30:19,000 --> 00:30:20,650
She died very young, didn't she?

332
00:30:22,630 --> 00:30:25,980
My brother sacrificed many things, Mr. Potter.

333
00:30:26,640 --> 00:30:28,350
On his journey to find power.

334
00:30:29,370 --> 00:30:30,490
Including Ariana.

335
00:30:31,740 --> 00:30:33,680
And she was devoted to him.

336
00:30:35,350 --> 00:30:36,620
He gave her everything,

337
00:30:38,890 --> 00:30:40,100
...but time.

338
00:30:41,980 --> 00:30:43,210
Thank you, Mr. Dumbledore.

339
00:30:51,170 --> 00:30:52,590
He did save our lives twice!

340
00:30:54,220 --> 00:30:55,330
Kept an eye on us on that mirror.

341
00:30:57,790 --> 00:30:59,580
That doesn't seem like someone who's given up!

342
00:31:06,090 --> 00:31:06,900
She's coming back.

343
00:31:08,950 --> 00:31:10,030
Who's that with her?

344
00:31:18,490 --> 00:31:19,230
Neville!

345
00:31:19,540 --> 00:31:21,150
- How you look... - Like hell, I reckon.

346
00:31:22,400 --> 00:31:23,050
This is nothing.

347
00:31:23,780 --> 00:31:24,580
Seamus is worse.

348
00:31:25,380 --> 00:31:26,310
Hey, Ab!

349
00:31:26,580 --> 00:31:27,980
We've got a couple more coming through.

350
00:31:30,430 --> 00:31:31,740
Don't remember this on the Marauder's Map.

351
00:31:32,350 --> 00:31:33,780
That's because it never existed till now.

352
00:31:34,460 --> 00:31:36,060
The seven secret passages were sealed off,

353
00:31:36,060 --> 00:31:37,170
before the start of the year.

354
00:31:37,800 --> 00:31:38,990
This is the only way in or out, now.

355
00:31:40,160 --> 00:31:42,030
The grounds are crawled with Death Eaters and Dementors.

356
00:31:42,650 --> 00:31:44,200
How about Mr.Snape as Headmaster?

357
00:31:44,440 --> 00:31:45,240
Hardly ever seen.

358
00:31:45,500 --> 00:31:47,010
It's the Carrows who's watch out for.

359
00:31:47,820 --> 00:31:48,360
Carrows?

360
00:31:48,640 --> 00:31:50,980
Yeah. Brother and sister. Incharge of discipline.

361
00:31:51,550 --> 00:31:52,740
They like punishment, the Carrows.

362
00:31:53,450 --> 00:31:54,160
They did that to you?

363
00:31:54,490 --> 00:31:55,610
Why?

364
00:31:55,610 --> 00:31:58,600
Today's Dark Arts lesson was practicing the Cruciatus curse.

365
00:31:59,440 --> 00:32:00,270
On first years.

366
00:32:01,510 --> 00:32:02,160
I refused.

367
00:32:04,120 --> 00:32:05,200
Hogwarts has changed.

368
00:32:19,080 --> 00:32:20,640
Let's have a bit of fun, shall we?

369
00:32:26,720 --> 00:32:28,290
Hey, listen up you lot!

370
00:32:28,880 --> 00:32:29,810
I've for you a surprise.

371
00:32:29,890 --> 00:32:31,630
No more Aberforth's cook gonna help.

372
00:32:32,280 --> 00:32:33,670
We'll be surprised if we can digest that.

373
00:32:36,590 --> 00:32:38,860
- Oh my! - Harry!

374
00:32:53,110 --> 00:32:55,260
Get the word out to Remus and the others, that Harry is back.

375
00:32:56,030 --> 00:32:56,740
Okay, okay!

376
00:32:57,270 --> 00:32:58,620
Let's not kill him before You-Know-Who does.

377
00:32:58,630 --> 00:33:00,560
Do you read? We've a new weather report.

378
00:33:00,560 --> 00:33:02,940
Lightning has struck. I repeat: Lightning has struck.

379
00:33:02,940 --> 00:33:03,600
What's the fun, Harry?

380
00:33:10,020 --> 00:33:10,680
Okay.

381
00:33:11,830 --> 00:33:13,150
There's something we need to find.

382
00:33:14,190 --> 00:33:16,070
Something hidden here, in the castle.

383
00:33:16,560 --> 00:33:18,270
And it may help us to defeat You-Know-Who.

384
00:33:19,270 --> 00:33:21,830
- Alright, what is it? - We don't know.

385
00:33:24,400 --> 00:33:26,340
- Where is it? - We don't know that either.

386
00:33:28,700 --> 00:33:29,830
I realize there's not much to go on.

387
00:33:29,950 --> 00:33:30,790
That's nothing to go on.

388
00:33:31,890 --> 00:33:33,780
I think it has something to do with Ravenclaw.

389
00:33:34,970 --> 00:33:38,890
It'll be small, easily concealed.

390
00:33:40,190 --> 00:33:41,400
Anyone, any ideas?

391
00:33:43,730 --> 00:33:46,030
Well, there's Rowena Ravenclaw's lost diadem.

392
00:33:46,270 --> 00:33:47,330
Oh, bloody hell! Here we go!

393
00:33:48,980 --> 00:33:50,480
Lost diadem of Ravenclaw?

394
00:33:51,630 --> 00:33:52,970
Hasn't anyone heard of this?

395
00:33:53,960 --> 00:33:54,880
It's quite famous.

396
00:33:55,580 --> 00:33:57,410
Yes. But, Luna, it's lost.

397
00:33:57,770 --> 00:34:01,220
For centuries. There's no person alive today who's seen it.

398
00:34:02,130 --> 00:34:03,950
Excuse me, can someone tell me what bloody diadem is?

399
00:34:04,470 --> 00:34:05,790
It's a sort of crown.

400
00:34:06,070 --> 00:34:07,090
You know, like a tiara.

401
00:34:10,450 --> 00:34:11,120
Harry!

402
00:34:12,730 --> 00:34:13,560
Hi, there.

403
00:34:17,480 --> 00:34:18,470
Six months she doesn't see me

404
00:34:18,470 --> 00:34:20,050
and it's like I'm a frankie first-year.

405
00:34:20,700 --> 00:34:21,450
I'm her brother!

406
00:34:21,450 --> 00:34:22,390
She's got lots of them,

407
00:34:22,390 --> 00:34:23,230
but she's got only one Harry.

408
00:34:23,230 --> 00:34:24,190
Shut up, Seamus!

409
00:34:25,150 --> 00:34:25,770
What is it, Ginny?

410
00:34:26,710 --> 00:34:30,050
Snape knows... he knows that Harry was spotted in Hogsmeade.

411
00:35:10,090 --> 00:35:12,150
Many of you are surely wondering,

412
00:35:12,150 --> 00:35:14,460
why I have summoned you at this hour.

413
00:35:17,900 --> 00:35:20,560
It's come to my attention, that earlier this evening...

414
00:35:23,060 --> 00:35:25,060
Harry Potter was sighted in Hogsmeade.

415
00:35:27,930 --> 00:35:28,630
Now...

416
00:35:29,800 --> 00:35:31,000
should anyone...

417
00:35:32,760 --> 00:35:38,080
student or staff attempt to aid Mr. Potter,

418
00:35:39,430 --> 00:35:43,120
they will be punished in a manner

419
00:35:43,120 --> 00:35:45,980
consistent with the severity of their transcription,

420
00:35:45,980 --> 00:35:47,440
further more...

421
00:35:48,860 --> 00:35:52,460
Any person found to have knowledge of these events...

422
00:35:54,810 --> 00:35:58,100
who fails to come forward...

423
00:35:59,770 --> 00:36:07,320
...will be treated as equally guilty.

424
00:36:10,380 --> 00:36:11,190
Another...

425
00:36:15,980 --> 00:36:20,200
If anyone in here has any knowledge of

426
00:36:20,200 --> 00:36:23,420
Mr. Potter's movements this evening.

427
00:36:26,650 --> 00:36:29,450
I invite them to step forward.

428
00:36:33,900 --> 00:36:35,180
Now!

429
00:36:50,440 --> 00:36:53,860
It seems, despite your exhaustive defensive strategies,

430
00:36:54,440 --> 00:36:56,840
...you still have a bit of security problem, Headmaster.

431
00:37:00,710 --> 00:37:02,420
I'm afraid it's quite extensive.

432
00:37:04,200 --> 00:37:06,070
How dare you stand where he stood?

433
00:37:08,090 --> 00:37:09,860
Tell them how it happened that night?

434
00:37:09,860 --> 00:37:11,870
Tell them how you looked him in the eye...

435
00:37:12,230 --> 00:37:14,810
A man who trusted you, and killed him.

436
00:37:15,260 --> 00:37:15,800
Tell them!

437
00:37:42,200 --> 00:37:42,790
Coward!!!

438
00:37:52,170 --> 00:37:54,000
Harry.

439
00:37:55,520 --> 00:37:56,150
Potter?

440
00:38:31,370 --> 00:38:36,240
I know that many of you will want to fight.

441
00:38:36,970 --> 00:38:42,250
Some of you may even think that to fight is wise.

442
00:38:42,480 --> 00:38:44,270
But this is folly.

443
00:38:45,980 --> 00:38:48,560
Give me Harry Potter.

444
00:38:49,860 --> 00:38:53,550
Do this and none shall be harmed.

445
00:38:53,980 --> 00:39:00,210
Give me Harry Potter, and I shall leave Hogwarts untouched.

446
00:39:00,530 --> 00:39:07,490
Give me Harry Potter, and you will be rewarded.

447
00:39:07,610 --> 00:39:10,270
You have one hour.

448
00:39:20,890 --> 00:39:23,810
What're you waiting for? Someone grab him!

449
00:39:33,410 --> 00:39:37,840
Students out of bed! Students out of bed!

450
00:39:38,570 --> 00:39:40,100
Students in the corridor!

451
00:39:40,100 --> 00:39:42,330
They're supposed to be out of bed,

452
00:39:42,330 --> 00:39:43,550
you blithering idiot!

453
00:39:46,990 --> 00:39:47,890
Sorry ma'am.

454
00:39:48,190 --> 00:39:49,840
As it happens, Mr. Filch...

455
00:39:49,840 --> 00:39:51,680
Your arrival is most opportune.

456
00:39:52,510 --> 00:39:54,490
If you would, I would like you please,

457
00:39:54,490 --> 00:39:58,900
to lead miss Parkinson and the rest of Slytherin house, from the hall.

458
00:39:59,180 --> 00:40:02,310
Exactly where is it I'll be leading 'em to, ma'am?

459
00:40:02,310 --> 00:40:03,820
The dungeons would do.

460
00:40:09,250 --> 00:40:11,610
I presume you have a reason for returning, Potter.

461
00:40:11,650 --> 00:40:12,770
What is it you need?

462
00:40:12,920 --> 00:40:15,560
Time, Professor. As much as you can get me.

463
00:40:16,340 --> 00:40:17,590
Do what you have to do.

464
00:40:17,590 --> 00:40:19,300
I'll secure the castle.

465
00:40:20,860 --> 00:40:21,410
Potter...

466
00:40:24,410 --> 00:40:25,340
It's good to see you.

467
00:40:27,020 --> 00:40:28,310
It's good to see you too, Professor.

468
00:40:29,930 --> 00:40:30,930
Hold the fort, Neville.

469
00:40:35,690 --> 00:40:36,690
Hurry up! Come on!

470
00:40:43,640 --> 00:40:44,600
Harry!

471
00:40:45,080 --> 00:40:46,390
Hermione and I've been thinking,

472
00:40:46,390 --> 00:40:47,990
it doesn't matter if we find a Horcrux.

473
00:40:48,440 --> 00:40:49,130
What do you mean?

474
00:40:49,370 --> 00:40:50,720
Unless we can destroy it.

475
00:40:51,050 --> 00:40:52,270
So, we were thinking...

476
00:40:52,280 --> 00:40:53,740
Well, Ron was thinking, it was Ron's idea.

477
00:40:53,740 --> 00:40:54,980
It's completely brilliant.

478
00:40:54,980 --> 00:40:57,230
You destroyed Tom Riddle's diary with a Basilisk's fang, right?

479
00:40:58,350 --> 00:41:00,530
Well, me and Hermione did remind where we might find one.

480
00:41:00,790 --> 00:41:01,350
Okay.

481
00:41:02,760 --> 00:41:03,760
Okay, but take this.

482
00:41:04,390 --> 00:41:05,690
That way, you can find me when you get back.

483
00:41:06,480 --> 00:41:07,370
Where're you going?

484
00:41:07,370 --> 00:41:09,600
Ravenclaw common room, gotta start somewhere.

485
00:41:16,480 --> 00:41:17,390
Harry!

486
00:41:18,380 --> 00:41:19,300
Harry!

487
00:41:20,020 --> 00:41:21,120
Let me get this straight, Professor...

488
00:41:21,720 --> 00:41:23,300
You're actually giving us permission to do this?

489
00:41:23,650 --> 00:41:25,320
That is correct, Longbottom.

490
00:41:25,920 --> 00:41:27,400
To blow it up! Boom!

491
00:41:27,400 --> 00:41:28,510
Boom!

492
00:41:29,070 --> 00:41:29,760
Wicked!

493
00:41:30,500 --> 00:41:31,930
But how on earth are we gonna do that?

494
00:41:32,610 --> 00:41:35,260
Why don't you confer with Mr. Finnigan?

495
00:41:35,260 --> 00:41:39,110
As I recall, he has a particular proclivity for pyro-technics.

496
00:41:39,110 --> 00:41:40,060
I can bring it down.

497
00:41:40,060 --> 00:41:41,530
That's the spirit! Away, you go.

498
00:41:43,330 --> 00:41:44,580
You do realize, of course,

499
00:41:44,580 --> 00:41:46,710
we can't keep out You-Know-Who indefinitely.

500
00:41:46,920 --> 00:41:48,850
That doesn't mean we can't delay him.

501
00:41:50,720 --> 00:41:53,230
And his name is Voldemort.

502
00:41:53,230 --> 00:41:55,080
Filius, you might as well use it.

503
00:41:55,080 --> 00:41:57,700
He's come to try to kill you, either way!

504
00:42:00,650 --> 00:42:03,400
Piertotum Locomotor.

505
00:42:19,460 --> 00:42:20,780
Hogwarts is threatened.

506
00:42:21,350 --> 00:42:23,800
Man the boundaries! Protect us.

507
00:42:23,800 --> 00:42:26,500
Do your duty to our school.

508
00:42:30,610 --> 00:42:33,190
I've always wanted to use that spell!

509
00:42:43,290 --> 00:42:44,440
Protego Maxima

510
00:42:44,440 --> 00:42:45,380
Fianto Duri

511
00:42:45,380 --> 00:42:46,750
Repello Inimigotum

512
00:42:46,750 --> 00:42:47,990
Protego Maxima

513
00:42:48,690 --> 00:42:50,160
Fianto Duri

514
00:42:50,990 --> 00:42:51,570
Repello...

515
00:42:51,570 --> 00:42:52,520
Protego Maxima

516
00:42:52,520 --> 00:42:53,650
Fianto Duri

517
00:42:53,650 --> 00:42:55,570
Repello Inimigotum

518
00:42:56,380 --> 00:42:57,410
Protego Maxima

519
00:43:25,810 --> 00:43:27,240
Harry, wait!

520
00:43:27,990 --> 00:43:29,030
I need to talk to you!

521
00:43:29,040 --> 00:43:30,250
I'm a bit pre-occupied at the moment,Luna.

522
00:43:30,260 --> 00:43:31,850
You don't know anything where you're going.

523
00:43:31,850 --> 00:43:32,790
You're wasting your time!

524
00:43:33,260 --> 00:43:34,580
Look, we'll talk later, okay, Luna?

525
00:43:34,580 --> 00:43:35,980
- Harry? - Later.

526
00:43:36,100 --> 00:43:38,370
Harry Potter, you listen to me right now!

527
00:43:40,650 --> 00:43:43,540
Do you remember what Cho said about Rowena Ravenclaw's Diadem?

528
00:43:44,030 --> 00:43:45,790
There is not a person alive who's seen it.

529
00:43:47,460 --> 00:43:48,540
It's obvious, isn't it?

530
00:43:49,300 --> 00:43:51,140
We have to talk to someone who's dead.

531
00:44:02,330 --> 00:44:03,830
It's very impressive, isn't it?

532
00:44:20,330 --> 00:44:23,070
If you've to find her, you'll find her down there.

533
00:44:23,180 --> 00:44:24,490
- Aren't you coming? - No.

534
00:44:24,760 --> 00:44:26,680
I think it's best if you two talk alone.

535
00:44:27,410 --> 00:44:28,420
She's very shy.

536
00:44:56,120 --> 00:44:57,350
You're the Grey Lady.

537
00:44:58,550 --> 00:45:00,070
The ghost of Ravenclaw tower.

538
00:45:00,440 --> 00:45:02,230
I do not answer to that name!

539
00:45:02,460 --> 00:45:03,990
No, I'm sorry, I'm sorry!

540
00:45:04,320 --> 00:45:05,480
It's Helena, isn't it?

541
00:45:06,070 --> 00:45:08,530
Helena Ravenclaw, Rowena's daughter.

542
00:45:09,710 --> 00:45:11,190
Are you a friend of Luna's?

543
00:45:11,800 --> 00:45:12,450
Yes.

544
00:45:13,690 --> 00:45:15,330
And she thought you might be able to help me.

545
00:45:18,130 --> 00:45:20,120
You seek my mother's diadem?

546
00:45:22,260 --> 00:45:23,010
Yes.

547
00:45:24,900 --> 00:45:25,610
That's right.

548
00:45:27,710 --> 00:45:29,150
Luna is kind.

549
00:45:29,750 --> 00:45:31,650
Unlike so many of the others.

550
00:45:32,510 --> 00:45:35,620
But she was wrong, I cannot help you!

551
00:45:40,240 --> 00:45:41,690
Wait, please!

552
00:45:44,330 --> 00:45:45,850
I want to destroy it!

553
00:46:24,440 --> 00:46:25,920
They never learn.

554
00:46:27,910 --> 00:46:29,110
Such a pity.

555
00:46:30,370 --> 00:46:32,300
But, My Lord...

556
00:46:33,860 --> 00:46:35,060
Shouldn't we wait?

557
00:46:43,200 --> 00:46:43,990
Begin!

558
00:47:05,330 --> 00:47:06,860
I thought you want to do it. Isn't it, Helena?

559
00:47:13,140 --> 00:47:14,270
You want to destroy it?

560
00:47:14,600 --> 00:47:17,480
Another swore to destroy it, many years ago.

561
00:47:18,060 --> 00:47:20,390
A strange boy with a strange name.

562
00:47:20,930 --> 00:47:21,600
Tom Riddle.

563
00:47:21,790 --> 00:47:22,860
But he lied.

564
00:47:23,630 --> 00:47:24,970
He's lied to many people.

565
00:47:25,090 --> 00:47:28,150
I know what he's done! I know who he is!

566
00:47:28,530 --> 00:47:31,610
He defiled it, with dark magic!

567
00:47:46,420 --> 00:47:47,790
I can destroy it.

568
00:47:48,170 --> 00:47:49,400
Once and for all.

569
00:47:52,050 --> 00:47:53,930
But only if you tell me where he hid it?

570
00:47:56,980 --> 00:48:00,350
You do know, where he hid it?

571
00:48:00,890 --> 00:48:01,800
Don't you, Helena?

572
00:48:04,360 --> 00:48:05,530
You just have to tell me.

573
00:48:08,200 --> 00:48:09,060
Please!

574
00:48:21,770 --> 00:48:23,120
Strange!

575
00:48:27,000 --> 00:48:29,150
You remind me of him a bit.

576
00:48:31,200 --> 00:48:34,300
It's here, in the castle.

577
00:48:35,340 --> 00:48:37,270
In the place where everything is hidden.

578
00:48:39,750 --> 00:48:40,910
If you have to ask...

579
00:48:41,450 --> 00:48:42,530
....you will never know.

580
00:48:44,460 --> 00:48:45,390
If you know...

581
00:48:46,060 --> 00:48:47,470
...you need only ask.

582
00:48:49,710 --> 00:48:50,440
Thank you!

583
00:49:04,280 --> 00:49:05,340
Tell Professor McGonagall.

584
00:49:05,340 --> 00:49:07,290
Remus and I will handle this side of the castle.

585
00:49:09,340 --> 00:49:10,030
Yes, sir!

586
00:49:14,450 --> 00:49:16,240
Hey Dean, on second thoughts,

587
00:49:17,240 --> 00:49:18,020
tell Professor McGonagall

588
00:49:18,020 --> 00:49:20,090
we might need one or two more wands this side.

589
00:49:22,610 --> 00:49:23,820
It is the quality of one's

590
00:49:23,820 --> 00:49:25,680
convictions that determine his success...

591
00:49:25,770 --> 00:49:27,410
...not the number of followers.

592
00:49:28,160 --> 00:49:29,000
Who said that?

593
00:49:30,420 --> 00:49:30,950
Me.

594
00:49:36,730 --> 00:49:37,610
You okay, Freddie?

595
00:49:38,980 --> 00:49:39,920
Yeah.

596
00:49:41,930 --> 00:49:42,640
Me too.

597
00:50:00,690 --> 00:50:01,790
Harry talks in his sleep.

598
00:50:02,440 --> 00:50:03,140
Do you know this?

599
00:50:05,260 --> 00:50:06,360
No, of course, not!

600
00:50:54,630 --> 00:50:57,770
Yeah? You and whose army?

601
00:51:18,060 --> 00:51:18,940
You do it.

602
00:51:19,260 --> 00:51:20,480
I can't.

603
00:51:20,480 --> 00:51:21,430
Yes, you can!

604
00:54:19,830 --> 00:54:20,620
Neville!

605
00:54:38,850 --> 00:54:39,690
That went well.

606
00:55:26,830 --> 00:55:30,960
Get inside! This way! Take cover! Take cover

607
00:55:49,130 --> 00:55:49,800
Stupefy

608
00:55:53,370 --> 00:55:57,050
Ginny, Neville! You alright?

609
00:55:57,050 --> 00:55:58,050
Never better!

610
00:55:58,050 --> 00:56:00,100
I feel like I can spit fire!

611
00:56:00,100 --> 00:56:01,700
Have you seen Luna up here?

612
00:56:01,700 --> 00:56:02,540
Luna?

613
00:56:02,540 --> 00:56:03,470
I'm mad for her.

614
00:56:03,470 --> 00:56:05,160
I think it's about time I told her

615
00:56:05,170 --> 00:56:06,970
since we'll probably both be dead by dawn.

616
00:56:11,850 --> 00:56:12,500
I know.

617
00:56:41,540 --> 00:56:43,630
Bloody hell! We'll never find him on this.

618
00:56:44,110 --> 00:56:45,160
Here he is!

619
00:56:45,410 --> 00:56:46,790
- Just now... - Brilliant!

620
00:56:47,110 --> 00:56:48,150
He just vanished.

621
00:56:48,870 --> 00:56:50,140
I just now I saw it.

622
00:56:53,590 --> 00:56:55,490
Maybe he's gone to the Room of Requirement.

623
00:56:55,530 --> 00:56:57,030
It doesn't show up on the map, does it?

624
00:56:57,070 --> 00:56:58,370
You said that last year.

625
00:56:59,330 --> 00:57:00,670
That's right, I....I did.

626
00:57:01,830 --> 00:57:02,440
Let's go.

627
00:57:04,240 --> 00:57:05,090
Brilliant!

628
00:57:11,600 --> 00:57:13,150
Come on!

629
00:59:05,330 --> 00:59:06,080
Well, well...

630
00:59:07,660 --> 00:59:08,890
What brings you here, Potter?

631
00:59:10,600 --> 00:59:11,610
I could ask you the same.

632
00:59:12,900 --> 00:59:14,100
You have something of mine.

633
00:59:15,910 --> 00:59:16,960
I'd like it back.

634
00:59:17,300 --> 00:59:18,550
What's wrong with the one you have?

635
00:59:18,710 --> 00:59:19,520
It's my mother's.

636
00:59:20,180 --> 00:59:21,430
It's powerful, but it's...

637
00:59:22,190 --> 00:59:23,140
...not the same.

638
00:59:24,220 --> 00:59:26,840
Doesn't quite understand me.

639
00:59:28,260 --> 00:59:29,010
You know what I mean?

640
00:59:30,510 --> 00:59:31,470
Why didn't you tell her?

641
00:59:34,130 --> 00:59:34,900
Bellatrix?

642
00:59:38,730 --> 00:59:39,790
You knew it was me.

643
00:59:41,290 --> 00:59:42,250
You didn't say anything.

644
00:59:43,140 --> 00:59:43,930
Come on, Draco!

645
00:59:45,140 --> 00:59:45,960
Don't be a prat.

646
00:59:46,700 --> 00:59:47,440
Do it!

647
00:59:49,100 --> 00:59:49,650
Easy!

648
00:59:51,750 --> 00:59:52,520
Expelliarmus.

649
00:59:53,470 --> 00:59:54,440
Avada Kedavra.

650
00:59:54,720 --> 00:59:55,480
Stupefy.

651
00:59:59,760 --> 01:00:01,980
This is my girlfriend, you bloody gits!

652
01:00:24,400 --> 01:00:25,330
Got it!

653
01:00:40,620 --> 01:00:43,080
Goyle's set the bloody place on fire!

654
01:01:50,630 --> 01:01:51,770
Come on! This way!

655
01:02:00,370 --> 01:02:01,310
We can't leave them!

656
01:02:02,320 --> 01:02:03,360
He's joking, right?

657
01:02:13,180 --> 01:02:15,890
If we die for them, Harry, I'm gonna kill you!

658
01:02:38,100 --> 01:02:38,690
Harry!

659
01:03:26,780 --> 01:03:27,770
My Lord?

660
01:03:27,770 --> 01:03:29,260
Avada Kedavra!

661
01:03:36,430 --> 01:03:40,050
Come Nagini, I need to keep you safe.

662
01:03:53,750 --> 01:03:54,750
It's the snake.

663
01:03:55,870 --> 01:03:57,170
And she's the last one.

664
01:03:57,570 --> 01:03:58,670
It's the last Horcrux.

665
01:04:05,780 --> 01:04:06,930
Look inside him, Harry.

666
01:04:08,540 --> 01:04:10,140
Find out where he is,

667
01:04:10,150 --> 01:04:11,550
if you find him, we can find the snake.

668
01:04:12,220 --> 01:04:13,180
And we can end this!

669
01:04:41,730 --> 01:04:42,710
My Lord...

670
01:04:44,230 --> 01:04:46,940
Might it be less...

671
01:04:48,530 --> 01:04:52,030
I should not be more prudent to call off this attack.

672
01:04:53,280 --> 01:04:55,170
Simply seek the boy.

673
01:04:55,370 --> 01:04:56,120
Yourself.

674
01:04:56,220 --> 01:04:59,370
I do not need to seek the boy...

675
01:04:59,780 --> 01:05:01,680
before the night is out,

676
01:05:01,680 --> 01:05:04,250
he will come to me! Do you understand?

677
01:05:05,960 --> 01:05:06,530
Look at me!

678
01:05:08,240 --> 01:05:11,370
How can you live with yourself, Lucius?

679
01:05:12,250 --> 01:05:13,050
I don't know.

680
01:05:16,360 --> 01:05:17,600
Go and find Severus.

681
01:05:19,440 --> 01:05:20,510
Bring him to me.

682
01:05:29,480 --> 01:05:30,510
I know where he is.

683
01:05:41,300 --> 01:05:42,070
Come on!

684
01:06:30,550 --> 01:06:31,150
No!

685
01:07:18,910 --> 01:07:21,190
You have performed extra-ordinary

686
01:07:21,190 --> 01:07:22,250
magic with this wand, My Lord,

687
01:07:22,260 --> 01:07:24,330
in the last few hours alone.

688
01:07:24,370 --> 01:07:24,990
No!

689
01:07:26,640 --> 01:07:33,540
No! I am extra-ordinary. But the wand resists me.

690
01:07:33,830 --> 01:07:36,530
There is no wand more powerful.

691
01:07:36,530 --> 01:07:39,230
Ollivander himself has said it.

692
01:07:40,010 --> 01:07:42,170
Tonight, when the boy comes.

693
01:07:42,170 --> 01:07:45,250
It will not fail you, I am sure of it.

694
01:07:47,730 --> 01:07:53,590
It answers to you, and you only.

695
01:07:54,610 --> 01:07:55,420
Does it?

696
01:07:59,050 --> 01:07:59,740
My Lord?

697
01:08:02,880 --> 01:08:06,150
The wand, does it truly answer to me?

698
01:08:08,890 --> 01:08:10,640
You're a clever man, Severus.

699
01:08:11,190 --> 01:08:12,440
Surely you must know...

700
01:08:15,330 --> 01:08:20,230
- ...where does its true loyalty lie? - With you.

701
01:08:21,690 --> 01:08:23,560
Of course, My Lord.

702
01:08:23,930 --> 01:08:27,730
The Elder Wand cannot serve me properly,

703
01:08:27,730 --> 01:08:30,870
because I am not its true master.

704
01:08:32,660 --> 01:08:36,950
The Elder Wand belongs to the wizard who killed its last owner.

705
01:08:44,040 --> 01:08:46,610
You killed Dumbledore, Severus.

706
01:08:48,560 --> 01:08:52,770
While you live, the Elder Wand cannot truly be mine.

707
01:08:55,350 --> 01:08:58,500
You've been a good and faithful servant, Severus.

708
01:08:59,860 --> 01:09:03,760
But only I can live forever.

709
01:09:08,270 --> 01:09:09,190
My Lord...

710
01:09:15,170 --> 01:09:17,230
Nagini, kill!

711
01:10:17,870 --> 01:10:18,940
Take it.

712
01:10:20,860 --> 01:10:24,450
Take it up, please!

713
01:10:25,390 --> 01:10:27,980
Give me something! Quickly, a flask. Anything!

714
01:10:47,140 --> 01:10:48,710
Take them to the Pensieve.

715
01:10:52,060 --> 01:10:53,230
Look at me.

716
01:10:59,870 --> 01:11:01,850
You really have your mother's eyes.

717
01:11:35,790 --> 01:11:39,330
You've fought valiantly,

718
01:11:40,880 --> 01:11:43,000
but in vain.

719
01:11:46,600 --> 01:11:49,640
I do not wish this.

720
01:11:49,640 --> 01:11:55,250
Every drop of magical blood spilled is a terrible waste.

721
01:11:55,250 --> 01:11:59,260
I, therefore command my forces to retreat.

722
01:11:59,260 --> 01:12:02,180
In their absence,

723
01:12:02,180 --> 01:12:05,100
dispose your dead with dignity.

724
01:12:06,670 --> 01:12:08,470
Harry Potter,

725
01:12:08,470 --> 01:12:12,340
I now speak directly to you.

726
01:12:12,340 --> 01:12:14,490
On this night,

727
01:12:14,490 --> 01:12:18,540
you have allowed your friends to die for you,

728
01:12:18,540 --> 01:12:20,760
rather than face me yourself.

729
01:12:20,760 --> 01:12:23,930
There is no greater dishonor.

730
01:12:23,930 --> 01:12:27,770
Join me in the Forbidden Forrest...

731
01:12:27,770 --> 01:12:30,270
...and confront your fate.

732
01:12:30,270 --> 01:12:33,270
If you do not do this,

733
01:12:33,270 --> 01:12:37,930
I shall kill every last man,

734
01:12:37,930 --> 01:12:40,450
woman and child

735
01:12:40,450 --> 01:12:44,540
who tries to conceal you from me.

736
01:13:04,550 --> 01:13:05,610
Where's everybody?

737
01:13:31,570 --> 01:13:32,900
Harry?

738
01:13:38,540 --> 01:13:42,820
Oh, come on! Don't be sad on it, she's passed.

739
01:13:44,840 --> 01:13:46,120
There, she's gone.

740
01:15:55,860 --> 01:15:57,640
Freak! Come here!

741
01:15:57,640 --> 01:16:00,520
I'm gonna tell mommy! You're freak!

742
01:16:01,020 --> 01:16:02,580
You're freak, Lily!

743
01:16:03,020 --> 01:16:03,840
Come here!

744
01:16:26,100 --> 01:16:29,310
She's jealous. She's ordinary and you're special.

745
01:16:29,680 --> 01:16:30,640
That's mean, Severus.

746
01:16:54,660 --> 01:16:55,950
Gryffindor!

747
01:17:04,240 --> 01:17:06,090
- Hi, I'm James. - Hi, I'm Lily.

748
01:17:11,810 --> 01:17:12,800
Just like your father.

749
01:17:15,820 --> 01:17:17,920
Don't say a word against my father!

750
01:17:26,880 --> 01:17:30,650
Servants and masters shall be reunited once more!

751
01:17:31,180 --> 01:17:32,050
Severus.

752
01:17:34,220 --> 01:17:35,390
No, don't kill me!

753
01:17:36,330 --> 01:17:38,560
The prophecy did not refer to a woman.

754
01:17:40,380 --> 01:17:42,780
It spoke about a boy born at the end of the July.

755
01:17:42,790 --> 01:17:44,640
Yes, but he thinks it's her son!

756
01:17:45,640 --> 01:17:48,110
He intends to hunt them down and to kill them.

757
01:17:48,970 --> 01:17:52,930
Hide him... hide them all. I beg you!

758
01:17:53,490 --> 01:17:56,080
What would you give me in exchange, Severus?

759
01:17:58,560 --> 01:17:59,300
Anything.

760
01:17:59,300 --> 01:18:00,220
Harry...

761
01:18:00,770 --> 01:18:02,490
Harry, you were so loved.

762
01:18:03,180 --> 01:18:07,440
So loved! Harry, mama loves you.

763
01:18:08,420 --> 01:18:09,860
Dadda loves you.

764
01:18:12,160 --> 01:18:13,440
Harry, be safe.

765
01:18:14,540 --> 01:18:15,540
Be strong.

766
01:18:15,550 --> 01:18:16,970
Avada Kedavra!

767
01:18:22,600 --> 01:18:26,230
You said you would keep her safe.

768
01:18:26,240 --> 01:18:27,750
Lily and James...

769
01:18:28,030 --> 01:18:30,460
..put their faith in the wrong person, Severus.

770
01:18:31,160 --> 01:18:32,090
Rather like you.

771
01:18:35,390 --> 01:18:36,720
The boy survives.

772
01:18:36,730 --> 01:18:38,920
He doesn't need protection, the Dark Lord has gone.

773
01:18:39,120 --> 01:18:40,740
The Dark Lord will return.

774
01:18:41,750 --> 01:18:44,590
And when he does, the boy will be in terrible danger!

775
01:18:46,520 --> 01:18:47,860
He has her eyes.

776
01:18:52,430 --> 01:18:54,860
If you truly loved her...

777
01:18:58,290 --> 01:19:02,340
No one, can know.

778
01:19:02,340 --> 01:19:05,000
I shall never reveal the best of you, Severus.

779
01:19:05,000 --> 01:19:06,210
Your word?

780
01:19:06,210 --> 01:19:08,930
Can you risk your life every day to protect the boy?

781
01:19:08,940 --> 01:19:11,090
He possesses no measurable talent,

782
01:19:11,090 --> 01:19:13,360
his arrogance rivals even that of his father

783
01:19:13,360 --> 01:19:14,870
and he seems to relish in his fame.

784
01:19:15,100 --> 01:19:17,270
Don't say a word against my father!

785
01:19:18,150 --> 01:19:22,060
James Potter, lazy, arrogant.

786
01:19:22,060 --> 01:19:25,440
- My father was a great man! - Your father was a swine!

787
01:19:27,490 --> 01:19:30,100
Drink it up, it will contain

788
01:19:30,100 --> 01:19:32,950
the curse to your hand, for the time being.

789
01:19:33,350 --> 01:19:36,220
- It will spread, Albus. - How long?

790
01:19:38,440 --> 01:19:39,610
Maybe a year.

791
01:19:42,880 --> 01:19:43,970
Don't ignore me, Severus.

792
01:19:45,830 --> 01:19:47,370
We both know Lord Voldemort

793
01:19:47,370 --> 01:19:49,660
has ordered the Malfoy boy to murder me.

794
01:19:52,030 --> 01:19:58,000
But should he fail, I should presume the Dark Lord will turn to you.

795
01:20:01,270 --> 01:20:04,090
You must be the one to kill me, Severus.

796
01:20:05,440 --> 01:20:07,040
It is the only way.

797
01:20:08,530 --> 01:20:12,770
Only then, will the Dark Lord trust you completely.

798
01:20:19,100 --> 01:20:20,570
It will come a time,

799
01:20:20,570 --> 01:20:22,970
when Harry Potter, must be told something.

800
01:20:25,600 --> 01:20:30,600
But you must wait, until Voldemort is at his most vulnerable.

801
01:20:31,210 --> 01:20:32,780
Must be told what?

802
01:20:34,350 --> 01:20:38,270
On the night, Lord Voldemort went to Godric's Hollow to kill Harry,

803
01:20:40,590 --> 01:20:42,890
and Lily Potter cast herself between them.

804
01:20:43,920 --> 01:20:45,780
The curse rebounded.

805
01:20:47,880 --> 01:20:50,960
When that happens, a part of Voldemort's soul

806
01:20:51,330 --> 01:20:55,580
latched itself onto the only living thing it could find.

807
01:20:56,540 --> 01:20:57,870
Harry himself.

808
01:21:00,290 --> 01:21:02,690
There's a reason Harry can speak with snakes.

809
01:21:04,120 --> 01:21:07,060
There's a reason he can look into Lord Voldemort's mind.

810
01:21:09,270 --> 01:21:15,380
A part of Voldemort lives inside him.

811
01:21:21,810 --> 01:21:27,460
So, when the time comes, the boy must die?

812
01:21:29,780 --> 01:21:33,330
Yes... yes. He must die.

813
01:21:52,310 --> 01:21:56,140
You've kept him alive, so he can die at the proper moment?

814
01:22:00,920 --> 01:22:03,520
You've been raising him like a pig for slaughter.

815
01:22:04,630 --> 01:22:07,800
Don't tell me now, that you've grown to care for the boy.

816
01:22:13,440 --> 01:22:15,850
Expecto Patronum.

817
01:22:27,800 --> 01:22:28,720
Lily!

818
01:22:32,490 --> 01:22:33,780
After all this time?

819
01:22:38,400 --> 01:22:39,540
Always.

820
01:22:45,680 --> 01:22:47,530
So, when the time comes,

821
01:22:48,980 --> 01:22:50,790
the boy must die?

822
01:22:51,850 --> 01:22:52,770
Yes.

823
01:22:53,940 --> 01:22:57,710
He must die. And Voldemort himself must do it.

824
01:22:59,000 --> 01:23:00,310
That is essential.

825
01:24:06,380 --> 01:24:08,720
- Where've you been? - I thought you went to the forest.

826
01:24:08,810 --> 01:24:09,960
I'm going there now.

827
01:24:10,450 --> 01:24:12,360
Are you mad? No...

828
01:24:14,490 --> 01:24:15,910
You can't give yourself up to him.

829
01:24:20,250 --> 01:24:21,350
What is it, Harry?

830
01:24:23,700 --> 01:24:24,800
What is it you know?

831
01:24:28,510 --> 01:24:30,210
There's a reason I can hear them.

832
01:24:31,710 --> 01:24:32,810
The Horcruxes.

833
01:24:35,450 --> 01:24:37,010
I think I've known for a while.

834
01:24:39,260 --> 01:24:40,700
And I think you have, too.

835
01:24:44,580 --> 01:24:47,030
- I'll go with you. - No, kill the snake.

836
01:24:48,360 --> 01:24:50,230
Kill the snake, and then it's just him!

837
01:26:10,780 --> 01:26:12,130
I'm ready to die.

838
01:26:54,250 --> 01:26:55,820
Resurrection Stone.

839
01:27:26,380 --> 01:27:28,990
You've been so brave, sweetheart.

840
01:27:33,570 --> 01:27:36,810
Why are you here? All of you.

841
01:27:40,250 --> 01:27:41,360
We never left.

842
01:27:51,450 --> 01:27:54,740
Does... Does it hurt?

843
01:27:55,570 --> 01:27:57,230
Dying?

844
01:27:58,640 --> 01:28:00,430
Quicker than falling asleep.

845
01:28:04,920 --> 01:28:06,150
You're nearly there, son.

846
01:28:07,050 --> 01:28:08,450
I'm sorry.

847
01:28:08,960 --> 01:28:11,420
I never wanted any of you to die for me.

848
01:28:14,080 --> 01:28:15,520
And, Remus, your son?

849
01:28:15,520 --> 01:28:18,580
Others will tell him what his mother and father died for.

850
01:28:20,240 --> 01:28:22,640
One day, he'll understand.

851
01:28:35,300 --> 01:28:36,370
You'll stay with me?

852
01:28:38,590 --> 01:28:40,200
Until the end.

853
01:28:41,530 --> 01:28:42,970
And he won't be able to see you?

854
01:28:43,680 --> 01:28:44,520
No.

855
01:28:46,670 --> 01:28:48,230
We're here, you see.

856
01:29:03,530 --> 01:29:05,080
Stay close to me.

857
01:29:07,710 --> 01:29:09,030
Always.

858
01:29:24,180 --> 01:29:27,180
No sign of him, My Lord.

859
01:29:43,520 --> 01:29:45,170
I thought he would come.

860
01:30:27,060 --> 01:30:29,080
Harry, no!

861
01:30:29,310 --> 01:30:31,770
- What're yeh doin' here? - Quiet!

862
01:30:43,230 --> 01:30:44,530
Harry Potter...

863
01:30:48,540 --> 01:30:50,290
The Boy Who Lived...

864
01:30:55,540 --> 01:30:57,090
come to die.

865
01:31:16,140 --> 01:31:18,690
Avada Kedavra.

866
01:32:14,230 --> 01:32:15,460
You can't help.

867
01:32:17,150 --> 01:32:20,140
Harry, you wonderful boy.

868
01:32:21,310 --> 01:32:24,080
You brave, brave man!

869
01:32:27,250 --> 01:32:28,420
Let us walk.

870
01:32:36,670 --> 01:32:38,060
Professor, what is that?

871
01:32:41,680 --> 01:32:43,910
Something beyond either of our help.

872
01:32:47,590 --> 01:32:50,010
A part of Voldemort sent here to die.

873
01:32:51,200 --> 01:32:52,520
And exactly where are we?

874
01:32:53,600 --> 01:32:55,270
I was going to ask you that.

875
01:32:55,900 --> 01:32:57,280
Where would you say that we are?

876
01:32:57,950 --> 01:33:01,310
Well, it looks like King's Cross station.

877
01:33:02,710 --> 01:33:04,220
Only cleaner,

878
01:33:05,110 --> 01:33:06,360
and without all the trains.

879
01:33:07,820 --> 01:33:09,750
King's Cross, is that right?

880
01:33:10,920 --> 01:33:13,870
This is, as they say, "your" party.

881
01:33:15,680 --> 01:33:18,200
I expect you now realize that you and Voldemort

882
01:33:19,110 --> 01:33:21,300
have been connected by something other than fate.

883
01:33:21,800 --> 01:33:24,720
Since that night in Godric's Hollow, all those years ago.

884
01:33:25,080 --> 01:33:26,500
So it's true then, sir.

885
01:33:27,070 --> 01:33:29,140
A part of him lives within me, doesn't it?

886
01:33:30,250 --> 01:33:31,190
Did.

887
01:33:31,390 --> 01:33:32,670
It's been just destroyed

888
01:33:32,670 --> 01:33:35,550
many moments ago by none other than Voldemort himself.

889
01:33:37,420 --> 01:33:41,230
You, were the Horcrux he never meant to make, Harry.

890
01:33:54,840 --> 01:33:58,230
- I have to go back, haven't I? - Oh, that's up to you.

891
01:33:58,430 --> 01:34:01,300
- I've a choice? - Oh, yes!

892
01:34:02,380 --> 01:34:04,160
We're in King's Cross, you say.

893
01:34:06,330 --> 01:34:08,020
I think if you so decide,

894
01:34:08,020 --> 01:34:10,750
you'll be able to board a train.

895
01:34:12,690 --> 01:34:14,360
And where would it take me?

896
01:34:15,350 --> 01:34:16,330
On.

897
01:34:35,090 --> 01:34:36,690
Voldemort has the Elder Wand.

898
01:34:40,050 --> 01:34:40,980
True.

899
01:34:40,990 --> 01:34:42,370
And the snake's still alive?

900
01:34:42,690 --> 01:34:43,550
Yes.

901
01:34:44,380 --> 01:34:45,880
And I've nothing to kill it with?

902
01:34:47,320 --> 01:34:49,450
Help will always be given at Hogwarts,

903
01:34:49,450 --> 01:34:51,160
Harry. To those who ask for it.

904
01:34:53,130 --> 01:34:56,660
I've always pride of myself on my ability to turn a phrase.

905
01:34:57,860 --> 01:35:00,180
Words are, in my not so humble opinion,

906
01:35:01,150 --> 01:35:04,030
are most inexhaustible source of magic.

907
01:35:05,080 --> 01:35:08,610
Capable of inflicting injury and remedies.

908
01:35:09,820 --> 01:35:14,990
But I would in this case, amend my original statement to this:

909
01:35:18,580 --> 01:35:22,190
Help, will always be given at Hogwarts,

910
01:35:22,190 --> 01:35:23,880
to those who deserve it.

911
01:35:30,610 --> 01:35:32,350
Do not pity the dead, Harry.

912
01:35:33,800 --> 01:35:34,990
Pity the living.

913
01:35:36,410 --> 01:35:40,270
And above all, all those who live without love.

914
01:35:42,260 --> 01:35:44,160
Professor, my mother's Patronus,

915
01:35:44,920 --> 01:35:47,310
was a doe, wasn't it?

916
01:35:48,720 --> 01:35:50,600
As the same as Professor Snape's.

917
01:35:52,120 --> 01:35:54,490
It's curious, don't you think?

918
01:35:54,490 --> 01:35:58,420
Actually, if I think about it, it doesn't seem curious at all!

919
01:36:01,160 --> 01:36:02,450
I'll be going now, Harry.

920
01:36:03,750 --> 01:36:04,800
Professor?

921
01:36:09,750 --> 01:36:11,050
Is this all real?

922
01:36:12,530 --> 01:36:14,430
Or is it just happening inside my head?

923
01:36:14,440 --> 01:36:17,010
Of course it's happening inside your head, Harry.

924
01:36:18,260 --> 01:36:21,120
Why should that mean, that it's not real?

925
01:36:27,570 --> 01:36:28,800
Professor?

926
01:36:29,370 --> 01:36:30,440
What should I do?

927
01:36:34,980 --> 01:36:36,070
Professor!

928
01:36:40,040 --> 01:36:42,240
My Lord, My Lord...

929
01:36:42,290 --> 01:36:43,280
Are you hurt?

930
01:36:43,790 --> 01:36:45,530
I don't need your help.

931
01:36:57,100 --> 01:36:59,690
The boy... Is he dead?

932
01:37:15,170 --> 01:37:16,170
Is he alive?

933
01:37:17,450 --> 01:37:18,860
Draco, is he alive?

934
01:37:46,370 --> 01:37:47,050
Dead.

935
01:39:14,990 --> 01:39:15,600
Who is that?

936
01:39:16,380 --> 01:39:17,350
Hagrid's carrying?

937
01:39:18,410 --> 01:39:19,430
Neville, who is it?

938
01:39:20,930 --> 01:39:25,520
Harry Potter... is dead!

939
01:39:25,530 --> 01:39:26,550
No!

940
01:39:26,780 --> 01:39:27,500
No!

941
01:39:27,500 --> 01:39:28,350
Silence!

942
01:39:32,900 --> 01:39:34,550
Stupid girl!

943
01:39:36,180 --> 01:39:38,920
Harry Potter... is dead!

944
01:39:39,820 --> 01:39:46,260
From this day forth... you'll put your faith in me.

945
01:39:56,740 --> 01:39:58,580
Harry Potter is dead!

946
01:40:03,950 --> 01:40:06,230
And now it's the time to declare yourself.

947
01:40:08,960 --> 01:40:10,640
Come forward and join us,

948
01:40:13,100 --> 01:40:14,770
or die!

949
01:40:21,070 --> 01:40:22,020
Draco!

950
01:40:27,580 --> 01:40:28,380
Draco.

951
01:40:32,380 --> 01:40:33,260
Draco.

952
01:40:37,040 --> 01:40:37,750
Come.

953
01:40:51,120 --> 01:40:53,220
Well done, Draco.

954
01:40:54,110 --> 01:40:55,160
Well done!

955
01:41:18,490 --> 01:41:20,920
Well, I must say I'd hoped for better.

956
01:41:25,750 --> 01:41:27,730
And who might you be, young man?

957
01:41:29,980 --> 01:41:31,080
Neville Longbottom.

958
01:41:37,170 --> 01:41:40,880
Well, Neville, I'm sure we can find a place for you in our rank.

959
01:41:40,910 --> 01:41:42,380
I'd like to say something.

960
01:41:49,480 --> 01:41:51,160
Well, Neville, I'm sure we'd

961
01:41:51,170 --> 01:41:53,990
all be fascinated to hear what you have to say.

962
01:41:58,300 --> 01:42:00,440
- Doesn't matter that Harry is gone. - Stand down, Neville!

963
01:42:00,650 --> 01:42:02,060
People die everyday!

964
01:42:04,980 --> 01:42:08,290
Friends, family.

965
01:42:11,190 --> 01:42:11,870
Yeah.

966
01:42:14,220 --> 01:42:15,480
We lost Harry tonight.

967
01:42:18,020 --> 01:42:18,970
He's still with us.

968
01:42:20,520 --> 01:42:21,320
In here.

969
01:42:23,430 --> 01:42:29,960
So as Fred, Remus, Tonks...

970
01:42:31,600 --> 01:42:32,420
All of them.

971
01:42:34,990 --> 01:42:36,870
They didn't die in vain.

972
01:42:42,350 --> 01:42:43,330
But you will.

973
01:42:43,950 --> 01:42:44,910
Because you're wrong!

974
01:42:46,160 --> 01:42:47,450
Harry's heart did beat for us.

975
01:42:48,260 --> 01:42:49,120
For all of us!

976
01:42:49,580 --> 01:42:50,660
It's not over!

977
01:42:55,270 --> 01:42:56,020
Confringo.

978
01:43:08,290 --> 01:43:09,070
Come on!

979
01:43:18,150 --> 01:43:19,430
All remain into the castle.

980
01:43:19,670 --> 01:43:20,800
We have to kill the snake.

981
01:43:21,900 --> 01:43:22,490
Neville!

982
01:46:16,980 --> 01:46:19,170
Not my daughter, you bitch!

983
01:46:53,020 --> 01:46:54,050
Hey, you were right,

984
01:46:56,180 --> 01:46:58,290
when you told Professor Snape that wand was failing you.

985
01:46:58,380 --> 01:46:59,150
It will always fail.

986
01:47:01,540 --> 01:47:03,140
I killed Snape!

987
01:47:03,140 --> 01:47:04,570
But what if the wand never belonged to Snape?

988
01:47:04,570 --> 01:47:07,230
What if its allegiance is always to someone else?

989
01:47:08,400 --> 01:47:09,270
Oh, come on, Tom...

990
01:47:09,800 --> 01:47:11,210
Let's finish this the way we started.

991
01:47:12,750 --> 01:47:13,420
Together!

992
01:48:12,980 --> 01:48:14,030
Die!

993
01:50:58,920 --> 01:51:00,510
Harry!

994
01:52:01,130 --> 01:52:02,250
Why didn't it work for him?

995
01:52:02,890 --> 01:52:03,830
The Elder Wand?

996
01:52:05,840 --> 01:52:07,340
It answered to somebody else.

997
01:52:08,690 --> 01:52:09,790
When he killed Snape,

998
01:52:09,790 --> 01:52:11,260
he thought the wand would become his.

999
01:52:11,460 --> 01:52:12,050
But the thing is...

1000
01:52:13,650 --> 01:52:15,970
The wand never belonged to Snape.

1001
01:52:16,050 --> 01:52:17,530
It was Draco, who disarmed

1002
01:52:17,530 --> 01:52:19,370
Dumbledore that night in the Astronomy tower.

1003
01:52:20,660 --> 01:52:23,660
From that moment on and the wand answered him.

1004
01:52:25,560 --> 01:52:29,690
Until, the other night when I disarmed Draco.

1005
01:52:30,420 --> 01:52:31,440
At Malfoy Manor.

1006
01:52:32,310 --> 01:52:33,290
So, that means...

1007
01:52:35,830 --> 01:52:36,610
It's mine!

1008
01:52:39,800 --> 01:52:42,200
- What should we do with it? - We?

1009
01:52:43,670 --> 01:52:44,990
Just saying, that's the Elder Wand.

1010
01:52:45,790 --> 01:52:47,510
The most powerful wand in the world.

1011
01:52:48,440 --> 01:52:50,940
With that, he'd be invincible.

1012
01:55:14,980 --> 01:55:15,670
Together.

1013
01:55:55,420 --> 01:55:56,570
- Bag? - Yeah.

1014
01:55:57,420 --> 01:55:58,140
Jumper?

1015
01:56:00,140 --> 01:56:00,930
I'm gonna miss you.

1016
01:56:02,940 --> 01:56:04,180
Here they come.

1017
01:56:19,970 --> 01:56:20,670
Dad?

1018
01:56:21,600 --> 01:56:23,350
What if I am put in Slytherin?

1019
01:56:26,480 --> 01:56:28,940
Albus Severus Potter.

1020
01:56:30,400 --> 01:56:32,950
You were named after two Headmasters of Hogwarts.

1021
01:56:34,080 --> 01:56:35,970
One of them was a Slytherin.

1022
01:56:35,970 --> 01:56:38,860
And he was the bravest man I've ever known.

1023
01:56:41,110 --> 01:56:42,920
But just say if I am...

1024
01:56:42,920 --> 01:56:45,310
Then Slytherin house will have gained

1025
01:56:45,310 --> 01:56:47,260
a wonderful young wizard.

1026
01:56:48,600 --> 01:56:52,150
But listen, if it really means that much to you,

1027
01:56:52,150 --> 01:56:53,380
you can choose Gryffindor.

1028
01:56:54,210 --> 01:56:56,580
The Sorting Hat takes your choice into account.

1029
01:56:57,710 --> 01:56:59,810
- Really? - Really.

1030
01:57:03,930 --> 01:57:05,720
- Ready? - Ready.

